{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375912-creating-talismans","id":1375912,"title":"Creating Talismans...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-21T02:02:08-07:00","id":1375912,"title":"Creating Talismans...","content":"Does crafting a talisman with Prime 4 in MtA20 require you to burn a permanent willpower point? Or does it fall under the caveat... that you don't have to pay xp for something you create.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling you have to pay the WP and therefore the xp... Am I right?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T07:02:20-07:00","id":1375954,"title":"","content":"Talismans require a Permanent Wiipower Point to create. BOS pg 161. This has been the case at least since FBDF (Forged by Dragons Fire)<br /> <br /> A Talismans is an extension of the Mage who created it and therefore a piece of him is required in the creation. <br /> <br /> It's also a small price to pay for an item that can cast affects on their own as it's the only way to work 2 magical effects in one turn. Though I cant remember if M20 mention this it can be found in FBDF and my group still uses that ruling for Talismins, as do many others I am sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T07:58:08-07:00","id":1375965,"title":"","content":"Talismans and Grimoires. This has always been true. <br /> <br /> As well, you must expend personal Quintessence on the effort, above and beyond the Quintessence that you incorporate into the Wonder. <br /> <br /> Both of these requirements can be waived by Technocrats crafting Devices or Principiae in Technocratic facilities set up for the purpose, though you still need to incorporate the usual Quintessence into the Wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T04:50:13-07:00","id":1376516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375912-creating-talismans?p=1375965#post1375965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talismans and Grimoires. This has always been true.<br /> <br /> As well, you must expend personal Quintessence on the effort, above and beyond the Quintessence that you incorporate into the Wonder.<br /> <br /> Both of these requirements can be waived by Technocrats crafting Devices or Principiae in Technocratic facilities set up for the purpose, though you still need to incorporate the usual Quintessence into the Wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this gets dissected and fleshed out more. To the point where we can figure out exactly what say a Traditon mage would need to establish to do the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T08:22:10-07:00","id":1376557,"title":"","content":"I can see why the Traditions would be irked that the Technocracy has access to a trick that the Traditions don't; it suggests the possibility that the Technocracy might actually be <i>right</i> about some things. So yeah; they'd want to figure out the secret and replicate it for themselves. <br /> <br /> I don't see it happening, though, for a simple reason: a Tradition mage would probably have to adapt something like the Technocratic paradigm to do this. In-game, it's essentially a manifestation of the technological innovation of the assembly line, a move away from Wonders being unique and personal creations and toward them being mass-produced. On a gaming level, it essentially serves as the Technocracy's compensation for its members not being able to Surpass their Instruments. <br /> <br /> As such, I would propose that if you want a Tradition mage who knows how to craft Grimoires and Talismans without spending Willpower or personal Quintessence on the effort, you need to adopt a mindset toward your Instruments that denies you the ability to Surpass them. Not just \u201cyou start Surpassing them later\u201d, as with Technomancers, but \u201cyou <i>never</i> Surpass them\u201d. <i>That's</i> the price that the Technocracy pays for its ability to crank out Devices from a factory one after the other for as long as their Primal Energy supply holds out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T10:33:47-07:00","id":1376583,"title":"","content":"Hmm that's some keen insight. But I can still see Tradition Mages working Assembly line style in a specific Workshop. I guess going by what you are saying if they were to do it, it would be very specific and limited. There may be some middle ground with being able to pull it off and not necessarily having to have the Never Surpass instruments clause. Their workshop could be aimed towards mass producing specific exotic ingredients and refinements. At some point they could probably make certain Talismans mass produced for infrastructure purposes, like an amulet that allows you to step sideways with a reflection or speak with your mentor with your thoughts. or matter making cauldron. I don't know though I'm still grocking some of the system and the Techies weren't my specialty. The old Techie Players Guide had a lot to be desired concerning how well it fleshed out their Paradigm and the nature of Technomancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T13:53:43-07:00","id":1376608,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that the following is my take on the matter, and may not be 100% compatible with canon. But then, <i>canon</i> arguably isn't 100% compatible with canon\u2026<br /> <br /> The core of the mage's worldview is that Magick is inherently personal: the mage can do what he does because he has an innate quality that lets him bend reality to his will. Everything else follows from that, including the crafting of a Wonder. As such, mass production of Wonders isn't something that's within his notion of How Things Work. Even Etherites and VAs have a belief in some sort of inner spark that empowers them, and as such each and every Talisman crafted is intensely personal and a supreme act of will \u2014 thus the expenditure of a dot of Willpower. <br /> <br /> You want mass-produced Wonders from a mage? That's what Trinkets, Charms, and Artifacts are for. Talismans aren't just Wonders; they're the pinnacle of Wonders: items that <i>can work magick on their own</i>. In their worldview, the only way for that to be possible is if the crafter imprints the Talisman with a bit of his own ability to work Magick. That's what the dot of Willpower and points of personal Quintessence represent. <br /> <br /> When that's your fundamental view about how magick works, mass production of Talismans is out of the question. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Technocrats have an entirely different worldview. To them, what others call \u201cmagick\u201d is inherent in the world around them, just waiting to be unlocked. What makes an Enlightened Scientist special isn't an innate ability to bend reality to his will; it's an insight into the secrets of the true functioning of reality. Instruments aren't an aid to one's effort to focus his will; they're the keys that are used to unlock nature's mysteries. That's why you can't dispense with them: it's the Procedures that are central to Science, not some innate quality of the person performing them. <br /> <br /> In <i>that</i> worldview, there's nothing all that unusual about a Device; it's \u201cmerely\u201d a Gadget that can be used over and over again. That makes the notion of being able to mass-produce them a reasonable possibility. <br /> <br /> That said, even they can't do it automatically. They need to set up an appropriate Technocratic facility to make it work \u2014 and <i>that</i> is a capability arguably unique to Primal Utility, a Sphere variant that's inherently tied to the Technocratic mindset. This is much like how Primal Ventures are unique to Primal Utility. <br /> <br /> But the fact that they can do it <i>at all</i> is one of the reasons why the Technocracy is in the position that it's in: its ability to mass-produce Devices (given a sufficient supply of Primal Energy, which Primal Ventures go a long way toward providing) is the reason why the Technocracy has access to the Requisitions Background and nobody else does: it has so many Devices stockpiled that it <i>can</i> lend them out to field agents on a mission-by-mission basis. And it has those stockpiles because of the factories that let it mass produce them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T14:33:35-07:00","id":1376612,"title":"","content":"Would creating a Fetish also require the WP-expenditure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","us