classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375912-creating-talismans?p=1376608#post1376608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that the following is my take on the matter, and may not be 100% compatible with canon. But then, <i>canon</i> arguably isn't 100% compatible with canon\u2026<br /> <br /> The core of the mage's worldview is that Magick is inherently personal: the mage can do what he does because he has an innate quality that lets him bend reality to his will. Everything else follows from that, including the crafting of a Wonder. As such, mass production of Wonders isn't something that's within his notion of How Things Work. Even Etherites and VAs have a belief in some sort of inner spark that empowers them, and as such each and every Talisman crafted is intensely personal and a supreme act of will \u2014 thus the expenditure of a dot of Willpower.<br /> <br /> You want mass-produced Wonders from a mage? That's what Trinkets, Charms, and Artifacts are for. Talismans aren't just Wonders; they're the pinnacle of Wonders: items that <i>can work magick on their own</i>. In their worldview, the only way for that to be possible is if the crafter imprints the Talisman with a bit of his own ability to work Magick. That's what the dot of Willpower and points of personal Quintessence represent.<br /> <br /> When that's your fundamental view about how magick works, mass production of Talismans is out of the question.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Technocrats have an entirely different worldview. To them, what others call \u201cmagick\u201d is inherent in the world around them, just waiting to be unlocked. What makes an Enlightened Scientist special isn't an innate ability to bend reality to his will; it's an insight into the secrets of the true functioning of reality. Instruments aren't an aid to one's effort to focus his will; they're the keys that are used to unlock nature's mysteries. That's why you can't dispense with them: it's the Procedures that are central to Science, not some innate quality of the person performing them.<br /> <br /> In <i>that</i> worldview, there's nothing all that unusual about a Device; it's \u201cmerely\u201d a Gadget that can be used over and over again. That makes the notion of being able to mass-produce them a reasonable possibility.<br /> <br /> That said, even they can't do it automatically. They need to set up an appropriate Technocratic facility to make it work \u2014 and <i>that</i> is a capability arguably unique to Primal Utility, a Sphere variant that's inherently tied to the Technocratic mindset. This is much like how Primal Ventures are unique to Primal Utility.<br /> <br /> But the fact that they can do it <i>at all</i> is one of the reasons why the Technocracy is in the position that it's in: its ability to mass-produce Devices (given a sufficient supply of Primal Energy, which Primal Ventures go a long way toward providing) is the reason why the Technocracy has access to the Requisitions Background and nobody else does: it has so many Devices stockpiled that it <i>can</i> lend them out to field agents on a mission-by-mission basis. And it has those stockpiles because of the factories that let it mass produce them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay that makes a lot of sense it does fit more for lesser wonders. Still it does feel that kind of should apply somewhat to Techies as well with Talisman level devices custom made for their Extraordinary Citizens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T22:54:52-07:00","id":1376666,"title":"","content":"It feels the Traditions version of it would be making Wonders in the form of Ingredients that can be turned into multiple other objects. Like a Blessing Ritual over the creation of a batch of special steel, burn the Will and expend some exotic components into the Steel batch as a whole, then divide it up into special swords and armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T22:57:57-07:00","id":1376669,"title":"","content":"Ingredients, as you put it, are more commonly known as Tass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T23:03:50-07:00","id":1376671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375912-creating-talismans?p=1376669#post1376669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ingredients, as you put it, are more commonly known as Tass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean like Primium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T08:13:41-07:00","id":1376716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375912-creating-talismans?p=1376671#post1376671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean like Primium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primium it's not a Wonder, though. It's more like a Trinket, you do it with Matter 5 power to create new materials.<br /> <br /> That being said, discovering and creating an array of different &quot;magical materials&quot; to create a complex item that's more Talisman than Trinket seems hard/convoluted enough as to not steal the thunder of the Technocracy, and cool enough that I could consider it a substitution for Will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}